# Cross-runtime validation of the cumulative substrate-attention stack
# in pure-OMC Prometheus. PyTorch already showed the stack winning at
# L1-MH on TinyShakespeare; v0.8.4 made it practical to run the same
# question in OMC at single-head, modest scale, multiple seeds.
#
# Four arms, all single-head transformer, same corpus / size / steps:
#   A. L0          standard QKV attention
#   B. L1+SMOD+V   substrate-K + S-MOD α=1.0 + substrate-V resample
#   C. + Q6 fused  adds tape_phi_log-based Q6 modulation (v0.8.1)
#   D. + Q6 composed  same math via tape_abs+tape_log (v0.8.1 reference)
#
# Reports per-seed losses + mean per arm. Hypothesis is the PyTorch
# directional ranking (A > B > C ≈ D) carries over to the OMC runtime.

import "examples/lib/prometheus.omc";

fn build_vocab(text) {
